<title>ITALY: Benetton '96 cons net profit up 11.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Benetton '96 cons net profit up 11.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		   245.7     vs   220.3</p>
<p>    Total revenues		  2,871.1     vs 2,939.1</p>
<p>    Operating profit		  401.7     vs   443.8</p>
<p>    Ordinary dividend	     500 lire    vs 425 lire</p>
<p>Note - Benetton group issued results in statement after board meeting.  </p>
<p>    Net financial position	 133	  (up 273)</p>
<p>    Net financial charges	   12.6	vs    46.6</p>
<p>    Net equity		     1,821	  (up 10 pct)</p>
<p>    Gross operating margin     1,154.5	vs 1,217.8</p>
<p>Note - Benetton said it had eliminated net debt for the first time in its history and ended 1996 with liquidity of 133 billion lire.</p>
<p>It said the light fall in turnover was down to a marked appreciation of the lira and divestment of non-strategic businesses.</p>
<p>Gross operating margin was 40 percent of sales, slightly less than the previous year when it was 41.4 percent.</p>
<p>Globally, sales volume was up nearly four percent with a rise in European markets, eastern European countries and some Middle Eastern countries.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
